<div class="mb-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Is this original research?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">No. It is a digest of published studies, news reports on them and regulator pages, all listed in the Sources section. Zunkiree Labs did not run a survey or collect data for it.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Which clinical AI result is the strongest?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">In this digest, the two randomized trials, the MASAI mammography trial and the UCLA ambient scribe trial, use the strongest designs. Each tested specific tools in specific settings and its authors or sources state limits.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Do the results mean AI is safe to use in clinical care?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">No. The digest reports what the studies found and where they stop. Notes contained errors in the scribe trial, and an independent check found one widely used sepsis model missed most cases. Safety depends on the tool, the setting and the oversight.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">How should a clinic use a digest like this?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Use it to ask better questions of suppliers: what evidence, from whom, measured how, and with what error and false-alarm rates. Then run a small supervised pilot.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

